rota lap 4621, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; law and boundary read through touch, whose instruction is to close a hand on a boundary and pull. Row 1 stood at one reading today against rows 0, 2 and 4 at two, and it is the derived row besides. It surfaced a named refusal that no line in this tree can make -- a fence post standing on the diagram and passing through under the hand.
think Round open adopted the anointed order at 4cedc471ab and named one session log standing in the dead-letter box and nowhere else. The cold roster pass was already in flight from a dead lap, so I read its transcript rather than opening a second.
think Reds first: the cold pass closed at 249 green with one red, stash_record records_unlanded=1, and the record it named was my own ship's lap of 20260911.043239 -- killed mid-send with a whole keystone staged and untracked in the stash.
think That log read status GREEN and named every file it produced, which is the status-before-the-send clause doing exactly the job it was seated for. A killed lap and a finished lap that declined to send would otherwise read identically from outside.
think I restored the stash and re-ran its witness on this tree before believing it: rye_build_lock_reach GREEN, 18 legs, build_roots=1314, cross_scope_collisions=0.
think Then the hot pass reddened it. The scan reads tracked tools/* for rye build and rye run invocations, and staging its own control put the control's planted lines into the population -- lock_scopes 2 to 5, naming lab, lab/deep and shared, cross_scope_collisions=1.
think The elder pen rule excluded a cd whose directory is a shell VARIABLE. This control writes literal directories into its pens, so nothing caught them. That is REDS %519's law in a second room: a control's plants are literal lines of the tree.
think I took the narrow repair rather than the class sweep. Measured: two other controls, rye_harness_roster_control.sh and rye_lib_resolve_control.sh, name genuine tracked sources, so excluding every _control.sh would hide real invocations to spare one.
think The same trap then closed on the repair's own head comment, whose example spelled a plant out in full -- so the scan counted its own documentation as a fourth lock scope. An illustration is written from placeholders for exactly this reason.
think The air row's own work: I pressed the reflex TAME states everywhere -- fail with a NAMED error -- and asked whether the promise reaches. Zig enforces one half, that a returned error belongs to the declared set, and nothing asks whether a declared member can ever arrive.
obs Measured over 1,965 tracked authored sources: 4,213 declared member sites, 1,472 distinct names, 10,070 productions, and nine sites naming a refusal no line in this tree can make -- four in Glow, five across Caravan, Mycelium, Rishi's matcher and the vault.
obs The per-file reading is a different question and is gated at nothing. Error names are global in Zig, so OweMisrecorded stands in 47 Caravan rungs and is returned in two; 165 of the 261 unreached sites are that one sound habit, and gating it would red the tree for a shared vocabulary.
obs Three of the four Glow names were left deliberately. 20260720-032713_stoa97-token-mold-spec.bron writes "remain in ParseError set (no removal); only their emission paths change". The decision was right and it stood in no instrument for fourteen months.
obs I did not take the removal. Narrowing a public error set changes what a caller may plan for even where the member is provably inert, and a prior hand's written decision outranks this lap's tidiness. The instrument is the lap; the cut is Keaton's word.
obs My own instrument was wrong twice before it was right. The extractor required a member line to end at the comma, so 409 members carrying a trailing comment were invisible -- population 3,805 to 4,213, dead reading unmoved, which is the honest shape of that repair.
obs An inline error set in a signature opened a block that stayed open. The clause closing it earns its place in a pen alone: this tree writes zero capitalized enum members across 573 enums, so the shape lives in the language while the corpus stays clear of it, and the mutation removing the clause costs two legs.
obs Folding three walks into one awk reader took the scan 11.7s to 7.6s over the same files with byte-identical output, which is what let it sit at tier lap rather than on the slower clock.
obs The hot close reproduced REDS %700 and gave it an observation it lacked. mantra_tablecloth_query_wire answered red inside the loaded roster pass and GREEN three times bare, seconds later, on the same tree. The row records its cause as inference rather than observation; what stands now is that the flap follows parallel load rather than tree state. The ledger cannot take the line -- the pin holds 40,960 of 40,960 bytes with every row OPEN -- so it is recorded here and on the card until the bound rises on Keaton's word.
obs Hot close: 255 guards run, 251 green, 2 red, 2 gated at custody %5, tree_moved=no. Both reds are that one flap and its red_self echo in standing_equipment. Cold open read 249 green with one red, the stash record this lap closed.
